error[keywords]: `int32` is a keyword and may not be used as an identifier
   ┌ test.idl:3:5
   │
 2 │ enum Type {
 3 │     INT32,
   ·     ^^^^^ this is an IDL keyword
 4 │     UInt64,
 5 │     OCTET
   └──
 help: the keyword can be escaped by changing to `_INT32`
 note: keywords are matched case-insensitively against identifiers

error[keywords]: `uint64` is a keyword and may not be used as an identifier
   ┌ test.idl:4:5
   │
 2 │ enum Type {
 3 │     INT32,
 4 │     UInt64,
   ·     ^^^^^^ this is an IDL keyword
 5 │     OCTET
 6 │ };
   └──
 help: the keyword can be escaped by changing to `_UInt64`
 note: keywords are matched case-insensitively against identifiers

